<title>USA: IMF to locate Asia, Pacific office in Tokyo.</title>
<headline>IMF to locate Asia, Pacific office in Tokyo.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Monetary Fund will establish its regional office for Asia and the Pacific in Tokyo, Managing Director Michel Camdessus said on Friday.</p>
<p>The fund has already announced that Kunio Saito, who is a native of Japan, will head the new office, which is expected to be open for business by late August.</p>
<p>&quot;The primary aims of establishing this office are to allow the IMF to develop closer ties with national policymakers in the region,&quot; Camdessus said in a statement released here.</p>
<p>((-- Washington Newsroom (202) 898-8300))</p>
</text>
